{
  "title": "[dynamo] add more debug information to LazyVariableTrackers",
  "issue_id": "162860",
  "bug_description": "LazyVariableTracker logs in `TORCH_LOGS=trace_bytecode` are opaque and don't provide much context.\n\nIt would be good to include information such as:\n- the type of the example value\n- If the variable has been realized, output the realized variable as well\n\nFor example,\n```python\nimport torch\n\n\ndef inner(x):\n    return x + 1\n\n\n@torch.compile(backend=\"eager\")\ndef fn(x):\n    x = inner(x)\n    return inner(x)\n\n\nfn(torch.ones(3))\n```\n\nToday, `TORCH_LOGS=trace_bytecode` gives:\n```\nTRACE RESUME 0 []\nTRACE LOAD_GLOBAL inner []\nTRACE LOAD_FAST x [LazyVariableTracker(), NullVariable]\nTRACE CALL 1 [LazyVariableTracker(), NullVariable, LazyVariableTracker()]\nTRACE RESUME 0 []\nTRACE LOAD_FAST x []\nTRACE LOAD_CONST 1 [TensorVariable()]\nTRACE BINARY_OP 0 [TensorVariable(), ConstantVariable(int: 1)]\nTRACE RETURN_VALUE None [TensorVariable()]\nTRACE STORE_FAST x [TensorVariable()]\nTRACE LOAD_GLOBAL inner []\nTRACE LOAD_FAST x [LazyVariableTracker(), NullVariable]\nTRACE CALL 1 [LazyVariableTracker(), NullVariable, TensorVariable()]\nTRACE RESUME 0 []\nTRACE LOAD_FAST x []\nTRACE LOAD_CONST 1 [TensorVariable()]\nTRACE BINARY_OP 0 [TensorVariable(), ConstantVariable(int: 1)]\nTRACE RETURN_VALUE None [TensorVariable()]\nTRACE RETURN_VALUE None [TensorVariable()]\n```\n\nWith better LazyVariableTracker logging, we could instead have:\n```\nTRACE RESUME 0 []\nTRACE LOAD_GLOBAL inner []\nTRACE LOAD_FAST x [LazyVariableTracker(type(value): <class 'function'>), NullVariable]\nTRACE CALL 1 [LazyVariableTracker(type(value): <class 'function'>), NullVariable, LazyVariableTracker()]\nTRACE RESUME 0 []\nTRACE LOAD_FAST x []\nTRACE LOAD_CONST 1 [TensorVariable()]\nTRACE BINARY_OP 0 [TensorVariable(), ConstantVariable(int: 1)]\nTRACE RETURN_VALUE None [TensorVariable()]\nTRACE STORE_FAST x [TensorVariable()]\nTRACE LOAD_GLOBAL inner []\nTRACE LOAD_FAST x [LazyVariableTracker(type(value): <class 'function'>, realized:UserFunctionVariable), NullVariable]\nTRACE CALL 1 [LazyVariableTracker(type(value): <class 'function'>, realized:UserFunctionVariable), NullVariable, TensorVariable()]\nTRACE RESUME 0 []\nTRACE LOAD_FAST x []\nTRACE LOAD_CONST 1 [TensorVariable()]\nTRACE BINARY_OP 0 [TensorVariable(), ConstantVariable(int: 1)]\nTRACE RETURN_VALUE None [TensorVariable()]\nTRACE RETURN_VALUE None [TensorVariable()]\n```\n\ncc @chauhang @penguinwu @voznesenskym @EikanWang @jgong5 @Guobing-Chen @XiaobingSuper @zhuhaozhe @blzheng @wenzhe-nrv @jiayisunx @chenyang78 @kadeng @amjames @Lucaskabela",
  "apis": [
    "torch",
    "torch.compile",
    "torch.ones"
  ],
